# REASON: harness reliability only; no scoring logic changed. (1) Adds a real subprocess
# timeout to the per-example inference call — previously unbounded, so a dead/unresponsive
# agent hung the whole batch forever with no way to recover. (2) Adds infer_only (skip ASR,
# write status="awaiting_scoring") to support running all inference first and scoring
# separately, so NeMo's CPU-heavy transcription never runs while the agent is live accepting
# job dispatches (the two together are the fix for the reliability problem in (1)/lk_agent_tool
# diff). (3) Fixes a genuine pre-existing bug in the ALREADY-SHIPPED --asr-only re-scoring mode:
# room_name/stream_start_time (needed for tool-call telemetry) were never restored from a prior
# result file, so any --asr-only re-run — with or without this session's two-phase split —
# would have silently returned empty actual_tool_calls for every scenario.
